PATCH 527: FUN_0000_0757 -- the arctangent-of-a-4-word-vector entry lost its DGROUP base.

SAUDI7's SIGSEGV (t=3906), the last of the three distinct faults behind the nine failing self-play
missions:

    #0 FUN_0000_0757 (param_1=0xca2a)   #1 FUN_0000_0749   #2 FUN_0000_902c
    #3 FUN_0000_c0e5   #4 FUN_0000_c0ca   #5 FUN_0000_459a

asm 0x757 (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00), verified against re_out/fist_dat_image.bin:

    757: 8b 47 04    mov ax,[bx+4]
    75a: 8b 57 06    mov dx,[bx+6]
    75d: 8b 4f 02    mov cx,[bx+2]
    760: 8b 1f       mov bx,[bx]
    762: eb 1a       jmp 0x77e            ; -> FUN_0000_077e(ax,cx,dx,bx), the patch-476 arctangent

BX is a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET -- 0xca2a here, threaded down from 902c.  Ghidra typed the parameter
`undefined2 *` and dereferenced it as a host address.  The argument order it recovered is correct;
only the base is missing.  This is the same defect patch 324 fixed in 3d4c, the other caller of 077e.

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -5378,7 +5378,14 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_0757(undefined2 *param_1)
 
 {
-  FUN_0000_077e(param_1[2],param_1[1],param_1[3],*param_1);
+  /* PATCH 527: the ARCTANGENT-of-a-4-word-vector entry (asm 0x757-0x763, DS=DGROUP=0x1c00):
+   *     757: mov ax,[bx+4] / mov dx,[bx+6] / mov cx,[bx+2] / mov bx,[bx] / jmp 0x77e
+   * BX is a DGROUP NEAR OFFSET (0xca2a on SAUDI7, passed down from 902c <- c0e5 <- c0ca), but Ghidra
+   * typed param_1 as `undefined2 *` and dereferenced it as a HOST pointer -> SIGSEGV at t=3906.  The
+   * argument ORDER Ghidra recovered is right (077e takes ax,cx,dx,bx = +4,+2,+6,+0); only the base was
+   * lost.  Same class as patch 324's fix of 3d4c, which is the other caller of 077e. */
+  uint16_t *p = (uint16_t *)(g_mem + 0x1c000 + (uint16_t)(uintptr_t)param_1);
+  FUN_0000_077e(p[2],p[1],p[3],p[0]);
   return;
 }
 
